Paragraph 2 builds on Paragraph 1 by considering a family of such grids parametrized by a shift t. This paragraph provides necessary details about how the grid is constructed, which contributes to understanding the hashing scheme but slightly less than Paragraph 1 as it's more specific and not introducing new concepts.

Paragraph 3 describes the two-stage construction of the hash function using the randomly shifted grids. This paragraph carries a significant portion of the scientific contribution, explaining how the curve is snapped to the grid and duplicates are removed. It provides essential details about the methodology used in this paper.

Paragraph 4 concludes by stating that \u03b4be the family of hash functions ht \u03b4constructed this way. This paragraph serves as a summary, which is important but less impactful than the other sections. It receives the lowest score among all four paragraphs.
