Parent: The percentage of similarity between these two strings is approximately 57%. This Parenting Style Hash Function (HS) scheme for speed-constrained LSH has a bi-criterion collision probability that depends on the w-speed Fr\u00e9chet distance and the traversal width.

The proof of Lemma 15 shows that if the w-speed Fr\u00e9chet distance between two curves P and Q is less than a threshold r, then there exists an optimal w-speed traversal with cost at most c = sqrt(d) * (2w/m)^(1/2), where d is the diameter of the space in which the curves are embedded.

The probability that all nodes of P and Q within components ci+1, . . . . , c(i+1) are contained in the i-th subsequence of PandQ (event E1,i) is 1 / (w*l)^2 for each 1 ≤ i ≤ v/m. This probability holds even when conditioning on event E1,i−1.

The proof continues as in Lemma 12, where the only difference is in the probability of event E1,i. Indeed, we have that event E1,1happens with probability 1 /(w*l)^2, that is when P1 and Q1 contain only the at most w nodes of PandQin the first l components. The same probability holds for E1,i, conditioning on E1,i−1.

The proof continues as in Lemma 16, where the only difference i s in the probability of event E2,i. Indeed, we have that event E2,i happens with probability 1 /(w*l)2, that is when P and Q contain only the at most w nodes of PandQin the (i+1)-th component. The same probability holds for E2,i, conditioning on E1,i−1.

The proof follows from Lemmas 15 and 16.
